                        "entry_id": "7eeb8706-b4d6-3146-898d-2d0c00add30e",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Of, pertaining to, or consisting of hair."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "not-comparable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "07c489fe-649e-4ae3-aab5-655a7e7ac724",
                                "sense_id": "831836c0-8a33-3acb-b988-b71e006fd974",
                                "text": "Another frequent affection of the labia majora, is vulvular folliculitis of Hulguier, that is to say the inflammatlon of the numerous pileous and sebaceous glands of this organ."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "1b884329-bc53-42d9-9dbd-05684c6cd4e3",
                                "sense_id": "831836c0-8a33-3acb-b988-b71e006fd974",
                                "text": "A thyroid lack is usually characterised by skin infiltration, by dryness and desquamation, by depletion of the pileous system,[…]."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "3f2ba701-40a1-4249-9be9-67c6c1fb7418",
                                "sense_id": "831836c0-8a33-3acb-b988-b71e006fd974",
                                "text": "The play is indeed dominated by disguise and linguistic mimicry as Titus, the \"carrot-headed\" comic hero, tries to overcome prejudice against redheads and climb the social ladder by donning a wig and pretending to be \"normal\" in matters pileous."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e6d1d599-b080-4401-ab48-2c6ab3b26189",
                                "sense_id": "831836c0-8a33-3acb-b988-b71e006fd974",
                                "text": "What pileous sculptures was the young man creating on that lovely head?"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "28d2f4d7-e6bb-372a-9e14-0d1b54c75e45",
                        "entry_id": "7eeb8706-b4d6-3146-898d-2d0c00add30e",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Covered with hair; hairy."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "comparable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "2c596b8c-8a23-4e64-bbe0-3cf13063bc9f",
                                "sense_id": "28d2f4d7-e6bb-372a-9e14-0d1b54c75e45",
                                "text": "This rare species might, but for the rugose and pileous epidermis and more depressed form, readily be confounded with the preceding."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d4925b31-7d23-44ce-abc4-28b4aefa654c",
                                "sense_id": "28d2f4d7-e6bb-372a-9e14-0d1b54c75e45",
                                "text": "One cannot help but wonder whether the concerns ultimately had root in the presence of a diminutive, pileous, and swarthy Mediterranean atop a military vehicle, instead of our accepted Anglo-Saxon image of leadership and might."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f5602e81-82d3-46b2-ac39-fc97dd014486",
                                "sense_id": "28d2f4d7-e6bb-372a-9e14-0d1b54c75e45",
                                "text": "All of her attention is focused on surveying the rippled surface of my sturdy, pileous torso. I encourage her by stroking down her hair."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
